# Available TODOS

## Agent workflow queue (added 2026-10-09; run through /ship-feature in this order)

- Migration runner — first feature through the agent workflow. Build a `migrations/` folder of chronological up/down SQL files plus a small runner (applied-migrations table, up, down, status), invoked via a package script. Until it exists, schema changes stay add-only idempotent DDL in src/backend/database/db.repo.ts with a written rollback note in the feature spec. Owner: database-engineer.

- Test infrastructure — second feature through the agent workflow. Approved: supertest, a throwaway test PostgreSQL, React Testing Library + happy-dom, Playwright. Requirements: keep `bun test` as the single runner for unit, API (supertest) and component (RTL + happy-dom) tests; do not rewrite or restyle existing tests; Playwright lives in its own `e2e/` folder with its own runner and `bun test` must not pick those files up; limit the happy-dom setup to component tests if possible; replace tests/bun-test.d.ts with @types/bun rather than extending the stub; add separate scripts for unit, integration and e2e; the current 89 tests must still pass unchanged after setup; show the result to the user. Until this lands, agents must state "TOOLING MISSING" in their reports for API/component/e2e/migration/restore tests instead of skipping them silently. Owners: qa-engineer (test config, fixtures) with backend-engineer for package.json dependency and script changes.

- HIGH PRIORITY: Audit-log trimming and clearing — first real product feature through the agent workflow. server.ts:97 (POST /api/audit-logs deletes rows beyond the newest 500), server.ts:131 (clearAuditLogsHandler runs TRUNCATE TABLE zmc_audit_logs), server.ts:142-143 (POST /api/audit-logs/clear and DELETE /api/audit-logs routes), plus the matching in-memory cache trim/clear. Audit logs must be append-only and tamper-evident with no edit or delete path, admin included. Known issue: reviewers block on it only when a change touches audit logging. Likely depends on the migration runner and test infrastructure.

- Doctor lab lists (views/doctor/_utils/doctor-catalog.ts) vs backend LAB_CATALOGUE — derive display groups from the canonical source so price drift becomes structurally impossible.

- Eye catalog (views/eye/_utils/eye-catalog.ts — EYE_TESTS / PROCEDURES / FRAMES / LENSES / ACCESSORIES, 26 items) vs the backend eye catalogue — same treatment: check whether a server-side canonical exists and whether the frontend copy should derive from it.

## Moved from docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN_GUIDE.md on 2026-10-09 (verified against the codebase; in document order)

- Auth hardening — remove plaintext seed passwords and default-password fallback: seeds still plaintext in src/backend/database/db.repo.ts (admin/admin123 and related seed rows) and src/backend/routes/auth/auth.repository.ts (compat users with admin123/opd123/cash123 and similar); src/backend/routes/auth/auth.service.ts still accepts direct-match plaintext plus a universal 'password' fallback. Keep bcrypt compare (cost 12) and migrate-on-write; force resets and delete the fallback.

- CORS allowlist — server.ts still falls back to permissive `origin: true` when CORS_ORIGIN is unset; restrict to the intranet origin and fail closed in production.

- Security middleware — no helmet-equivalent headers, no login rate-limiting, no zod validators in package.json; add all three.

- Maintenance endpoint role checks — server.ts:146 (POST /api/maintenance/cache-clear), server.ts:263 (POST /api/maintenance/vacuum) and server.ts:322 (GET /api/db-test, which returns connection config and table counts) use authenticateJWT only, with no authorizeRoles, so any logged-in user of any role can call them. Add authorizeRoles(['IT Administrator']) to match the it_admin-only maintenance rule in the design guide, audit each call, and cover role denial with a regression test. Also tighten the endpoints that already check roles but admit 'Administrator' alongside 'IT Administrator': server.ts:155 (POST /api/maintenance/clear-store), server.ts:211 (POST /api/maintenance/system-reset), server.ts:294 (GET /api/maintenance/backup) and server.ts:409 (POST /api/db-test/seed) — restrict them to IT Administrator. Restricting by name is not enough on its own: src/backend/middleware/auth.middleware.ts:41-44 (ROLE_EQUIVALENTS) treats Administrator, IT Administrator, Management and Super Administrator as interchangeable, and line 65 lets all four bypass every authorizeRoles check, so Management currently passes any maintenance or clinical role check. Add a strict it_admin-only check for maintenance that ignores the equivalence map and bypass, and review whether the bypass should exist at all (it conflicts with the role-permission matrix, where it_admin never edits clinical or billing content). Owner: backend-engineer.

- LAN TLS termination — no https.createServer or certificate handling in server.ts; add private certificate authority plus Nginx TLS front, HSTS with HTTP redirect, and wss-only WebSocket.

- ON DELETE CASCADE on clinical foreign keys — src/backend/database/db.repo.ts has 44 ON DELETE CASCADE foreign keys (first at around lines 495, 513-514, 525, 531: patient vitals, maternity and emergency records), declared with `REFERENCES zmc_patients(id) ON DELETE CASCADE` / `zmc_encounters(id) ON DELETE CASCADE`, so deleting a patient or encounter silently destroys clinical history. Switch clinical, financial and audit foreign keys to ON DELETE RESTRICT (with soft delete) via the migration runner. Owner: database-engineer.

- Explicit column lists — `SELECT *` still used across the application (payments, patients, hr, nursing, exports routes and db.repo.ts refreshCache); replace with explicit column lists per the migration and security sections.

- Dynamic SET column whitelist — src/backend/routes/users/users.repository.ts builds `SET ${setClause}` from arbitrary request keys and src/backend/routes/patients/patients.repository.ts falls back to the raw key when unmapped; whitelist updatable columns in validators.

- Kobo money migration — nothing in src/ uses amount_kobo yet; floats persist (CARD_FEES constants, card_fee NUMERIC columns, 3000.00 literals); migrate money to *_kobo BIGINT with round-half-up, a reconciliation report, and a single formatKobo helper at the UI edge.
  - REMINDER (added 2026-10-10): plan the streamlined kobo conversion implementation before building. Inputs: the two deliverables documents in docs/internal (Kelechi_Deliverables.docx, Taiwo_Deliverables.docx) and the analysis shared on 2026-10-10 (<https://claude.ai/share/6ace458f-237d-439b-926b-c3857ba52fca>), summarised below. Billing and schema change, so it goes through the full path (/ship-feature); it depends on the migration runner. Principle: kobo is the only unit past one boundary layer (naira in only at the admin price form, naira out only at formatKobo).
    - Column shape: every money column becomes `*_kobo BIGINT NOT NULL CHECK (>= 0)` — zmc_invoices amount/amount_paid/balance (there is no total_amount column; that name is only an in-memory nursing handover field), zmc_payments amount/total_bill/balance, zmc_outstanding_balances total_bill/amount_paid/balance, zmc_emergency_records total_bill/cash_collected, plus catalogue prices (price_kobo). This also fixes the history.outstanding vs outstandingBalances and total_amount/amount field-mismatch bugs (same root cause). The database evaluation (docs/delivery-plan/day-02/qa-db-evaluation.md, 2026-10-10) counts about 40 money columns across about 20 tables, including zmc_lab_payments, patients.outstanding_balance and card_fee (INT), laboratory_orders.price, the four discount-request amounts, no_charge_records.treatment_cost, family, company, payment vitae, eye and price_catalogue — all DECIMAL(x,2) or INT, so ×100 is exact. It recommends expand-then-contract on the billing core (invoices, payments, outstanding balances, discounts, lab payments, emergency records) before Day 4 rather than one atomic rename before Day 3. Note: no fee_catalogue table exists today; catalogue prices live in src/backend/catalogue, so decide whether price_kobo is a code constant or a new table.
    - Backfill: one migration converts legacy naira ×100 (round-half-up) with a per-row before/after reconciliation report. It is the only place naira→kobo conversion of existing data happens; no ad hoc conversions in bug-fix PRs.
    - Catalogue: single source of truth in kobo. Any admin price-edit form takes naira and converts in exactly one service function.
    - Billing logic: pure integer kobo math (totals, discounts, balances). Grep for `* 100` / `/ 100` inside billing code; each hit is a misplaced conversion to remove.
    - Validators: payment/invoice endpoints accept integer `amountKobo` only and reject decimals, to stop a client sending 5000.00 naira instead of 500000 kobo.
    - types.ts: kobo-only DTOs; delete the naira-named and dual amount/amount_paid spellings rather than keeping both.
    - refreshCache: add the renamed `_kobo` columns to the snake_case→camelCase mapping, or the UI loses them while the DB is correct.
    - Frontend: replace all manual formatting (string concatenation, `/100`, `.toFixed(2)`) with one shared formatKobo() helper.
    - Sequencing: schema rename + backfill + validator change land as one atomic migration BEFORE the 15-day sprint's Days 3–6 payment-isolation fixes (e.g. the partial-payment OR-predicate bug), so those fixes are written once against the final schema.

- Automatic discount application — the approve handler (payments.routes.ts discount-requests approve) trusts the cashier-computed final_amount and writes it straight to the invoice; add the immutable discount_applications row with server-side recompute plus broadcast to cashier.

- Discharge absorption linking — no DISCH- invoice logic exists; link absorbed lines via absorbed_into_discharge_id with AbsorbedIntoDischarge status (never mark Paid) and replace the hardcoded discharge_bill fallbacks in nursing.routes.ts.

- Eye billing unification — eye patients live in separate zmc_eye_patients / zmc_eye_consultations tables with no invoice link (see the no-invoice comment in patients.routes.ts eye section); route eye charges through standard invoices and review nursing dispensing/injection record linkage to patient plus encounter.

- Prototype store decommission — localStorage stores still live (pharmacy stock/procurement/admitted/queue, eye patients/consultations, cashier eye references); migrate one domain at a time to PostgreSQL behind the feature flag, then remove the fallback and block production seeding without written approval.

- Pricing-review wiring — the pricing-review module and zmc_pricing_review table exist but no order path returns 422 UNKNOWN_CODE or writes a review row; wire catalogue-code validation into lab, pharmacy, and eye order paths.

- Silent-default price alias removal — lab-catalogue.ts maps generic names ('Liver Function Test (LFT)', 'Electrolyte, Urea, Creatinine (E/U/C)') to the comprehensive SKUs; force an explicit standard/comprehensive pick with no silent default.

- refreshCache pagination — refreshCache runs full-table SELECT * with no LIMIT or OFFSET; switch list reads to paginated scoped queries and add indexes on patient_id, encounter_id, and status.

- server.ts module extraction — server.ts (562 lines) still carries inline audit-log, clear-store, and system-reset handlers; extract to maintenance and audit-log modules mounted before the Vite/static middleware.

- Oversize file splits on touch — db.repo.ts (~2,315 lines), nursing.routes.ts (~2,427), payments.routes.ts (~2,081), hr.routes.ts (~1,124), exports.routes.ts (~874) all still over the 500-line threshold; split by domain when touched.

- Bun script migration — package.json dev/build/start scripts still use tsx and node; switch to the Bun invocations (bun server.ts, bun dist/server.cjs) and drop tsx from the runtime path.

